  "scope": "The native installed lane authenticates the reviewed full inherited checked-record package selection for c, cpp. The full API checks valid, normalized, invalid parent, invalid child, alias, nested Fin, repeated-constructor and recovery cases before projecting proof-free results. Two independent author builds, source removal, offline installation, relocation and unchanged caller replay are retained where the host permits them. Hosted GitHub Linux x64 acceptance with an explicit glibc 2.38 package floor and load ceiling 12. Four ordinary/reviewed full/result-only selections reproduce complete C and C++ packages from two author roots, install offline after author removal, and replay unchanged independent C11/GMP and C++20 callers after physical relocation. Parent and child constructors, repeated positions with different constructor selections, nested inheritance, aliases and invalid inner and outer values are exercised; result-only packages erase input-constructor metadata. Complete original C and C++ archives, receipts, caller sources, execution records, the original TAP, the hosted verification and the exact producer source closure are retained. External compiler and operating-system distributions are not retained. Other hosts, callbacks and owned positions require separate evidence. This archive does not itself promote support. Inherited checked-record acceptance covers only the tested acyclic Span → Ticket → Stamped chain, its Ticket alias, repeated direct parameters, nested parent constraints and proof-free Ticket/Stamped results. Value-carrying receiver-dependent inherited fields, generic or recursive inheritance, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed.",
