  "scope": "The browser installed lane authenticates the ordinary result-only inherited checked-record package selection for node-javascript, node-typescript, browser-javascript, browser-react, browser-worker. The result-only API projects proof-free inherited Ticket and Stamped results without checked-input metadata. Two independent author builds, source removal, offline installation, relocation and unchanged caller replay are retained where the host permits them. The fixture covers inherited parent subobjects, child checked fields, aliases, nested inheritance, repeated constructor selections and constructor-free results. Ordinary and independently reviewed sources are exercised in full and result-only npm packages. Node JavaScript, strict TypeScript, Chromium, Firefox and WebKit execute source-free installed packages; browser contexts cover plain pages, React production and StrictMode, and dedicated workers. Complete component/runtime npm archives, installed receipts, reports, controls, TAP streams and browser observations are retained. Browser binaries and generated deployment directories are represented by their recorded identities and observations. The evidence applies to the exact Linux x64 Node and browser versions recorded in this index. Other hosts require independent installed acceptance. The hosted workflow serializes the four route/mode selections and caps Lean, compiler and build parallelism; peak memory and constructor-dispatch counts are not measured. This archive establishes installed npm/browser behavior, not promotion into the public support inventory. Inherited checked-record acceptance covers only the tested acyclic Span → Ticket → Stamped chain, its Ticket alias, repeated direct parameters, nested parent constraints and proof-free Ticket/Stamped results. Value-carrying receiver-dependent inherited fields, generic or recursive inheritance, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed.",
