  "scope": "The jvm installed lane authenticates the ordinary result-only inherited checked-record package selection for java, kotlin. The result-only API projects proof-free inherited Ticket and Stamped results without checked-input metadata. Two independent author builds, source removal, offline installation, relocation and unchanged caller replay are retained where the host permits them. The fixture covers inherited parent subobjects, child checked fields, aliases, nested inheritance, repeated constructor selections, and constructor-free results. Ordinary and independently reviewed sources are exercised in full and result-only Maven packages through independent Java and Kotlin callers. Complete Maven packages are reproduced, installed offline, executed before and after relocation, and reduced to source-free runtime deployments. Complete package archives, receipts, inventories, probes, execution records, TAP, controls, and producer/checker/archive source closures are retained. The package floor is glibc 2.38; the archive records and verifies the hosted runner's independently observed glibc and JVM tool identities. Compiler, operating-system, JDK, Kotlin compiler, Maven-format archive, and glibc distributions remain trusted inputs. This archive establishes installed JVM behavior, not promotion into the public support inventory. Inherited checked-record acceptance covers only the tested acyclic Span → Ticket → Stamped chain, its Ticket alias, repeated direct parameters, nested parent constraints and proof-free Ticket/Stamped results. Value-carrying receiver-dependent inherited fields, generic or recursive inheritance, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed.",
