  "scope": "The dotnet installed lane authenticates the ordinary full inherited checked-record package selection for dotnet. The full API checks valid, normalized, invalid parent, invalid child, alias, nested Fin, repeated-constructor and recovery cases before projecting proof-free results. Two independent author builds, source removal, offline installation, relocation and unchanged caller replay are retained where the host permits them. The fixture covers inherited parent subobjects, child checked fields, aliases, nested inheritance, repeated constructor selections, and constructor-free results. Ordinary and independently reviewed sources are exercised in full and result-only NuGet packages. Complete NuGet packages are reproduced, restored offline, executed before and after relocation, and reduced to source-free runtime deployments. Complete package archives, receipts, inventories, probes, execution records, TAP, controls, and producer/checker/archive source closures are retained. The package floor is glibc 2.38; the archive records and verifies the hosted runner's independently observed glibc and .NET identities. Compiler, operating-system, .NET SDK, shared-framework, NuGet, and glibc distributions remain trusted inputs. This archive establishes installed .NET behavior, not promotion into the public support inventory. Inherited checked-record acceptance covers only the tested acyclic Span → Ticket → Stamped chain, its Ticket alias, repeated direct parameters, nested parent constraints and proof-free Ticket/Stamped results. Value-carrying receiver-dependent inherited fields, generic or recursive inheritance, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed.",
