  "scope": "The wit installed lane authenticates the reviewed result-only inherited checked-record package selection for wit-wasi. The result-only API projects proof-free inherited Ticket and Stamped results without checked-input metadata. Two independent author builds, source removal, offline installation, relocation and unchanged caller replay are retained where the host permits them. The fixture covers inherited parent subobjects, child checked fields, aliases, nested inheritance, repeated constructor selections, and constructor-free results. Ordinary and independently reviewed sources are exercised in full and result-only WIT/WASI component packages. Complete packages are reproduced from two author roots, installed offline, exercised before and after relocation, and checked at a glibc 2.38 release floor. The generated C host requires its packaged native Lean component runtime; it is not a standalone WASI command. Complete archives, receipts, source-free inventories, caller binaries, execution records, TAP, and producer/checker/archive source closures are retained. Compiler, operating-system, wasm-tools, Wasmtime, and C toolchain distributions remain trusted inputs. This archive establishes installed WIT/WASI behavior, not promotion into the public support inventory. Inherited checked-record acceptance covers only the tested acyclic Span → Ticket → Stamped chain, its Ticket alias, repeated direct parameters, nested parent constraints and proof-free Ticket/Stamped results. Value-carrying receiver-dependent inherited fields, generic or recursive inheritance, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed.",
